==English==

===Etymology===
{{cal|en|la|atra bilis|ātra bīlis}}, itself a calque of {{der|en|grc|μελαγχολία}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|historical}} One of the four [[humour]]s of ancient and mediaeval [[physiology]], that was believed to be secreted by the [[kidney]]s and [[spleen]] and to cause [[melancholy]] and sadness when present in excess.
#: {{syn|en|melancholy}}
#: {{cot|en|yellow bile|phlegm|blood}}
#* {{RQ:Wollstonecraft Mary|passage=But these various pursuits did not banish all her cares, or carry off all her constitutional '''black bile'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=w:Siddhartha Mukherjee|title=The Emperor of all Maladies|page=49|publisher=Fourth Estate
|passage=The problem with treating cancer surgically, Galen suggested, was that '''black bile''' was everywhere, as inevitable and pervasive as any fluid.}}

